{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","text":"AsyncQueue","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8Trackers17ConsentDropReportO","text":"ConsentDropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/ConsentDropReport"},{"text":"> { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reports wait until they are read. A record dropped for room is reported as it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dropped; while that report waits unread, later ones merge into it, one report counting"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them all across their timestamps. So the reports waiting unread hold at most one overflow","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report between any two others (denials and finished trackers), however many events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overflow. The sequence ends once the consent is gone and every report has been read.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One task reads the reports at a time. The first iterator to read holds them until its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iteration ends or it is released; a second reader meanwhile waits its turn, logging a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"warning once, then reads on from the next report, so the first gets every report in order.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A reader cancelled while it waits returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Consent"]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/trackers\/consent\/dropreports"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8Trackers7ConsentV11dropReports11AsyncQueues0E5QueueVyAA0B10DropReportOGvp","symbolKind":"property","title":"dropReports","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Trackers\/Consent.swift#L117","fileName":"Consent.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"Trackers"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncQueue","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsentDropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:8Trackers17ConsentDropReportO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"A report of each drop of held or recovered records, in the order they happen.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Consent\/dropReports","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/trackers","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker app code tracks events with, and what it applies to each event before it is delivered: enrichers, samplers and consent."}],"type":"topic","title":"Trackers"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers/ConsentDropReport":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ConsentDropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ConsentDropReport","url":"\/d